---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { ENTITY } from "../data/legal";

const UPDATED = "2026-10-12";
---

<LegalLayout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How MedicSupport Network collects, uses and protects personal data about clinicians, clients and visitors."
	updated={UPDATED}
>
	<p>
		This policy explains how {ENTITY.tradingName} ("we", "the group") handles
		personal data. It applies to this website and to the personal data we process as an
		employer and as an operator of healthcare facilities.
	</p>

	<h2>Who we are</h2>
	<p>
		The data controller is <strong>{ENTITY.name}</strong>, trading as {ENTITY.tradingName}.
		Registered in {ENTITY.registration}, with our registered office at {ENTITY.address}.
	</p>
	<p>
		We are a hospital and clinic group. We <strong>employ our own clinicians</strong> and
		operate our own licensed facilities. We are not a recruitment agency and we do not sell
		or trade personal data.
	</p>

	<h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
	<h3>Clinicians and staff</h3>
	<p>
		To employ someone and to place them in a clinical role we must hold their identity,
		qualification, registration and health-related records. This includes application and
		recruitment records, identity documents, professional registration numbers, verified
		references, qualifications, mandatory health screening, immunisation status, and the
		employment and placement history of our own staff.
	</p>
	<p>
		<strong>Special category data.</strong> Health screening and occupational health records
		are special category data. We process them because clinical roles require fitness
		practitioner determinations and statutory health screening, and because patient safety
		depends on knowing who is fit to practise.
	</p>
	<p>
		<strong>Secondments.</strong> Where we second one of our own clinicians to a hospital in
		Europe or America, the receiving employer processes their data under its own
		responsibility. We share only what that placement requires, and the transfer is covered
		by appropriate safeguards — see below.
	</p>

	<h3>Patients</h3>
	<p>
		Where we operate a facility we process patient records as the provider of the care. That
		is governed primarily by the healthcare law and regulator of the country the facility is
		in, and this policy does not override it. Patient data is governed by clinical
		confidentiality rules, not merely by this website policy.
	</p>

	<h3>Clients, partners and website visitors</h3>
	<p>
		We hold business contact details for employers and partners who approach us about
		secondment, and enquiry details for people who contact us. For website visitors we hold
		server logs (IP address, browser type, requested page, timestamp) for security and
		diagnostics.
	</p>

	<h2>Lawful bases</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Contract</strong> — for staff and for clients we are under contract with.</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Legal obligation</strong> — statutory record keeping, professional registration,
			health and safety duties, and tax and employment law in each country we operate in.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Public interest</strong> — for the parts of health data necessary to deliver
			care safely and to operate a licensed facility.
		</li>
		<li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — security logging and fraud prevention.</li>
		<li><strong>Consent</strong> — for optional marketing, where you have asked for it.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>International transfers</h2>
	<p>
		We operate across Africa and Asia and second staff to Europe and America. Personal data
		therefore moves between countries with different data protection laws. Each transfer is
		made under an appropriate safeguard — adequacy regulations where they apply, otherwise
		standard contractual clauses — supported by a transfer risk assessment and technical and
		organisational controls. Access is granted per placement, not by default.
	</p>

	<h2>How long we keep data</h2>
	<p>
		Employment and clinical records are retained for the period required by the employment,
		health and regulatory record-keeping rules of the country concerned, which is typically
		substantially longer than an ordinary business record. Enquiry data that does not lead to
		an engagement is deleted within 24 months. Server logs are retained for up to 90 days.
	</p>

	<h2>Your rights</h2>
	<p>Where the law that applies to you provides them, you may have the right to:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>access your personal data and receive a copy;</li>
		<li>correct data that is inaccurate or incomplete;</li>
		<li>request erasure where there is no overriding legal reason to keep it;</li>
		<li>restrict or object to certain processing;</li>
		<li>receive data you gave us in a portable format;</li>
		<li>complain to your local data protection authority.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We do not delete clinical or registration records on request where we are legally
		required to retain them, and we will explain why if that applies to your request.
	</p>

	<h2>Security</h2>
	<p>
		Access to personnel and clinical records is restricted to those who need it for their
		role, is individually attributable, and is logged. Credentials that appear on this site
		are published only where the individual has been verified for that purpose.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Data protection queries: <a href={`mailto:${ENTITY.dpoEmail}`}>{ENTITY.dpoEmail}</a>.
		General enquiries: <a href={`mailto:${ENTITY.generalEmail}`}>{ENTITY.generalEmail}</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Changes</h2>
	<p>
		We will update the date at the top of this page when this policy changes. Material
		changes affecting how we use your data will be notified directly where we have your
		contact details.
	</p>
</LegalLayout>